  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "UET: fix TSS with entropy header",
  "description": "When the entropy header is present in the packet, the dissection function does not take into account the offset of this header. So it parses this header as the start of the TSS.\nThis commit fixes this behavior and we have correct parsing over UDP and over IP.\n\nTo reproduce, attached is a pcap with IP/UDP/TSS and IP/Entropy/TSS: [uether_tss_entropy.pcap](/uploads/2d28d8e46a34b73c8d9aaa2b94b5449e/uether_tss_entropy.pcap)\n\nThe frame before the fix:\n![wrong_tss_entropy_pkt](/uploads/fb686dfe18e821415e923ad1e7d057d0/wrong_tss_entropy_pkt.png){width=895 height=288}\n\nThe frames after the fix:\n\n* IP/Entropy/TSS\n![patched_tss_entropy_pkt](/uploads/20fb3c2a4d8a18e7f0432363d59c2463/patched_tss_entropy_pkt.png){width=895 height=288}\n\n* IP/UDP/TSS\n![patched_tss_udp_pkt](/uploads/b9bf729e1f6e54a7d13a2379f3c72707/patched_tss_udp_pkt.png){width=895 height=288}",
